{{!--
	link-mage-focus-as-items — one Focus pick (Paradigm / Practice / Instrument): a name and a
	description toggle, "like a Merit" (design D3, `link-mage-focus-as-items`).

	NOT `feature_item.hbs`. That partial is shared by twelve blocks across three tabs and carries a
	drag handle, an `isactive` checkbox, rollable dice/difficulty columns and a point-value column —
	a Focus pick has none of those, and suppressing four things with flags in a partial that busy
	would put its other twelve callers at risk for this one caller's shape.

	NOT `feature_item.hbs`'s / `stats_feature_row.hbs`'s eye icon either, and that is a discovery
	recorded here rather than papered over. Both of those rows' inline `.description` panel was
	REMOVED by `open-item-window-from-eye-icon` (2026-07-31): their eye now opens the item's own
	read-only `ItemViewer` in a SEPARATE WINDOW (`_handleCollapsibleClick`, pc-actor-sheet.js), not
	an inline reveal. So there is no still-existing inline toggle on those rows left to copy.

	What this row reuses instead is the OTHER disclosure this tab already has: the native
	`<details>`/`<summary>` `templates/actor/v3/feature.hbs` (the "Personaje" tab bio's splatfield
	prose merged into, add-pc-sheet-v3 §8.1/§8.2 — this row lives in the same section) uses to collapse
	a long splatfield prose box — `.v3-prose` / `.v3-prosesummary` / `.v3-prosechevron` /
	`.v3-proselabel` / `.v3-prosebody`, all already declared and scoped in `css/pc-actor-v3.css`. It is
	a genuine existing mechanism in this repo, not an invented one, and it is what actually satisfies
	"reveals the description in place, collapsed by default": no JavaScript at all, keyboard-operable
	natively, and its CLOSED state occupies exactly the same height for a 14,000-character description
	as for an empty one — the acceptance check this change is measured against.

	`item.enrichedDescription`/`item.hasDescription` are set once per render by `enrichFocusItems`
	(pc-actor-sheet.js), the SAME resolver (`resolveDescription`) the eye-icon viewer itself uses —
	live from the compendium when the item carries provenance and no override, its own stored text
	otherwise.

	`data-itemid` carries no `data-action` of its own — nothing on this row writes to the actor — but
	it is what every other row-shaped partial in this system stamps (`feature_item.hbs`,
	`stats_feature_row.hbs`), so a future edit/delete affordance for a Focus pick has somewhere to
	hang one, and it is the ONLY offline evidence `test-part-render.mjs`'s orphan sweep has that a
	SPECIFIC item (not merely its block) reached the page.
--}}
<details class="v3-prose v3-focusitem" data-itemid="{{item._id}}">
	<summary class="v3-prosesummary">
		<i class="fa-solid fa-angles-right v3-prosechevron" aria-hidden="true"></i>
		<span class="v3-proselabel splatFont" title="{{item.name}}">{{item.name}}</span>
	</summary>
	{{#if item.hasDescription}}
		<div class="v3-prosebody">{{{item.enrichedDescription}}}</div>
	{{else}}
		<div class="v3-prosebody information-area">{{localize 'wod.notes.descriptionmissing'}}</div>
	{{/if}}
</details>
